9. Separate data models from presentation and serialization using the Visitor Pattern

   Separate the shit from the cinnamon: data model classes previously mixed state representation with console formatting (`to_console`) and JSON serialization (`to_dict`). Refactored the result hierarchy to accept visitors so presentation and serialization live in dedicated, decoupled components.

   [x] 'content/test/results.py': Add Visitor dispatch methods to result model classes
       - Removed `to_dict` and `to_console` methods from domain models (`RunResult`, `AssertSuiteResult`, `MethodResult`, `ContainerResult`, `AtomicTestResult`, `FileAnalysisResults`, `FileReport`, `ExpectanceResult`, `SandboxOperationsResult`)
       - Implemented `accept(self, visitor)` on each result node to support double-dispatch traversal across the result tree

   [x] 'content/test/console_visitor.py': Implement ConsoleReportVisitor for terminal presentation
       - Created `ConsoleReportVisitor` to walk the result tree and accumulate formatted string output for terminal display
       - Replicated per-suite summaries, total/passed/failed/crashed test counts, import check results, and status icons
       - Formatted `RunResult` header by stripping `Run<` and `>` wrappers for clean execution labels (e.g., `Test results - YYYY.MM.DD.HH.MM`)

   [x] 'content/test/json_visitor.py': Implement JsonSerializerVisitor for dict and report serialization
       - Created `JsonSerializerVisitor` to recursively transform the result node tree into serializable dictionaries
       - Preserved exact field mappings and dictionary key structures required for downstream report file storage

   [x] 'content/test/html_visitor.py': Implement HtmlReportVisitor for interactive dashboard generation
       - Created `HtmlReportVisitor` to generate a self-contained, interactive single-file HTML report with embedded CSS styling and light JS interactivity
       - Added header stat boxes (Total, Passed, Failed, Crashed, Import Errors), quick filter toggles ("All Results" / "Failures & Crashes Only"), and collapsible suite and test sections
       - Built detail views for test expectances, execution frames (shell commands + exit codes), pre-/post-sandbox operations, and crash stack messages

   [x] 'content/test/orchestrators.py': Update GateInspector to delegate to visitors
       - Updated `GateInspector._write_report_file` to generate and persist both JSON (`.json`) and interactive HTML (`.html`) reports via `run_result.accept()`
       - Updated `GateInspector.write_console_report` to utilize `ConsoleReportVisitor` via `run_result.accept()` for terminal output

